format 1
adapter chat 1
npc: shrodi

node chat-shrodi-greeting
kind: greeting
pose: greet
title: Chat

    Hi, I'm Shrodi, your guide in AtomIQ!

    Ask me what to learn next, how something works, or for a quick quiz.

reply: What should I do next? -> chat-shrodi-next
reply: Explain something -> chat-shrodi-explain
reply: Quiz me -> chat-shrodi-quiz
reply: Show me around -> chat-shrodi-around
reply: Bye for now -> chat-shrodi-bye

node chat-shrodi-menu
kind: reply
pose: idle

    What else can I help with?

reply: What should I do next? -> chat-shrodi-next
reply: Explain something -> chat-shrodi-explain
reply: Quiz me -> chat-shrodi-quiz
reply: Show me around -> chat-shrodi-around
reply: Bye for now -> chat-shrodi-bye

node chat-shrodi-next
kind: reply
pose: point

    Your next lesson is waiting on the map.

    Shall I take you there?

link: Take me there => next-lesson
reply: Maybe later -> chat-shrodi-menu

node chat-shrodi-explain
kind: reply
pose: explain

    Sure! Pick something and I'll show you where to read about it.

reply: The atom -> chat-shrodi-atom
reply: Isotopes -> chat-shrodi-isotope
reply: Radioactive decay -> chat-shrodi-decay
reply: Half-life -> chat-shrodi-half-life
reply: Something else -> chat-shrodi-menu

node chat-shrodi-atom
kind: reply
pose: explain

    Everything is made of atoms.

    At the middle of each is a tiny nucleus of protons and neutrons, with electrons far outside it.

link: Open the nucleus in AtomDex => entry nucleus
reply: Back -> chat-shrodi-explain

node chat-shrodi-isotope
kind: reply
pose: explain

    Isotopes are atoms of one element with different numbers of neutrons.

    Same protons, so the same element. A different mass.

link: Open isotopes in AtomDex => entry isotope
reply: Back -> chat-shrodi-explain

node chat-shrodi-decay
kind: reply
pose: explain

    Some nuclei are unstable, so they change on their own and give off radiation.

    That change is called decay.

link: Open decay in AtomDex => entry decay
reply: Back -> chat-shrodi-explain

node chat-shrodi-half-life
kind: reply
pose: explain

    A half-life is how long it takes for half of a radioactive sample to decay.

    It can be a fraction of a second or billions of years.

link: Open half-life in AtomDex => entry half-life
reply: Back -> chat-shrodi-explain

node chat-shrodi-quiz
kind: reply
pose: cheer

    Ready for a quick round? Myth Buster is a fast one.

link: Start the round => mythbuster
reply: Not now -> chat-shrodi-menu

node chat-shrodi-around
kind: reply
pose: point

    This is your phone.

    Chats is where your teachers write to you, AtomDex is the encyclopedia, and new apps arrive as you learn.

link: Open AtomDex => app atomdex
link: Open Field Notes => app field-notes
reply: Back -> chat-shrodi-menu

node chat-shrodi-bye
kind: sign_off
pose: proud

    Any time. I'm right here in your phone.
